// Title: Base64 MZ Header In CommandLine
// Sigma ID: 22e58743-4ac8-4a9f-bf19-00a0428d8c5f
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-07-12 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects encoded base64 MZ header in the commandline
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2022/07/11/select-xmrig-from-sqlserver/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_inline_base64_mz_header.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "TVqQAAMAAAAEAAAA" or ProcessCommandLine contains "TVpQAAIAAAAEAA8A" or ProcessCommandLine contains "TVqAAAEAAAAEABAA" or ProcessCommandLine contains "TVoAAAAAAAAAAAAA" or ProcessCommandLine contains "TVpTAQEAAAAEAAAA"
